lines+=['','Full required Section 5 checks include S072 and S076; the source-bound expanded matrix distinguishes eligibility, required response information, optional material and post-award terms. All occurrences, not only selected IDs, are checked for exact quotation and complete anchor. Both arms face the same rebuilt strict structural gate. Actual reply boundaries are separately checked against the 150-bullet budget. Raw full rebuilt replies are copied byte-for-byte under `rebuild/run-results/scope-repair-full/` with local binary Git attributes.','','## Preservation, remaining risk and delivery','',f"Integrity audit: {verification['preserved_prior_files']} prior tracked files preserved (changed candidate/report paths have exact before snapshots). Original, verbatim feedback, frozen questions, all failed trials and previous review evidence are unchanged. All {verification['local_prior_artifacts_verified']} existing local sealed artifact files retain their hashes. The complete Git history remains; no amend, reset, force push or history rewrite was used.",'','This closes the specified warning failures on the frozen controls; it does not establish a general personal-content classifier. New activity wording can still produce conservative false warnings; unfamiliar obligation wording can still escape a finite heuristic. The validator does not prove semantic routing, issuer authority, packet-to-PDF fidelity or authenticity. Context stays protected until an explicit private heading, which favors missed-risk detection and may over-warn on poorly separated attachments. Strict validation detects copying failures but cannot guarantee the model will not make them. One trial per source/arm is a receipt, not a reliability estimate. Original Claude Sonnet/Opus conditions are not reproduced. Eligibility remains unverified.','', 'The prior warning-release delivery failure and repaired launcher proof remain unchanged under warning-repair/delivery-attempt-1 and dist/warning-release. Current offline audits execute the unchanged legacy, final-repair and warning-repair assertions at their own sealed commits in sibling clones, then run the current scope-repair audit.', '', 'Local package target: `dist/scope-release/`, including source ZIP, complete-history Git bundle, SHA256SUMS, RELEASE and fresh-clone FINAL_VERIFICATION. Packaging checks integrity/compliance separately from the measured performance above; a package audit pass does not erase a model failure. Older `dist/release/` and failed delivery attempts remain intact. `SUBMISSION_COMMENT.md` is still a draft; no public link, push or comment has been published.']
